# Declares this app's process types for Procfile-based platforms (Heroku, Render, Railway, etc.)
# and, more importantly, documents for anyone reading this repo that the `worker` process type
# is NOT optional — it MUST run as its own process/dyno/service in production, separate from the
# `web` process. See src/jobs/worker.process.js's header comment: the BullMQ booking worker is
# split into its own entry point specifically so it can be scaled independently of the HTTP API
# under load, and so the two can be started/stopped/restarted without affecting each other.
#
# Commands below mirror package.json's "start" and "worker" npm scripts exactly (see
# package.json's "scripts" block) — kept as direct `node` invocations here rather than `npm run
# ...` because most Procfile-reading platforms exec these commands directly, without npm in the
# path or performing its own script-lookup overhead.
web: node src/server.js
worker: node src/jobs/worker.process.js
